WEBVTT

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.212
Shh! Don't wake up Fry.

00:00:30.881 --> 00:00:33.966
Shh!
My roommate's sleeping!

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:37.428
Wake up already!
Huh?

00:00:37.554 --> 00:00:40.223
I'm about to get down and funky with this ladybot,

00:00:40.307 --> 00:00:42.141
and I'd appreciate
it if as many people

00:00:42.226 --> 00:00:43.976
as possible
could know about it.

00:00:44.061 --> 00:00:46.562
Now can we get
some privacy?

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.989
Oh, yeah!
Back it on up.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.666
Hambone, hambone!

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.501
Hambone

00:01:08.585 --> 00:01:11.754
Okay, hambone break's over.
Back to the bedroom!

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:16.843
Hambone, hambone!

00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:18.553
Hambone

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:25.518
Wake up
and feel the coffee!

00:01:27.271 --> 00:01:29.313
No, I'm late
for work again!

00:01:33.277 --> 00:01:34.360
Sorry I'm late.

00:01:34.444 --> 00:01:38.072
Well, well, well. Look who decided to show up.

00:01:38.156 --> 00:01:40.366
I've had it with
your tardiness, Fry.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.953
I expect you to arrive the
same time as everyone else.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:46.539
Well, wait a second.
Leela's not here yet.

00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:47.748
She left a while ago.

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:50.334
She said some idiot was taking
her to lunch for her birthday.

00:01:51.295 --> 00:01:52.461
Oh, no, I'm late!

00:01:59.887 --> 00:02:03.556
Since you got stood up, I thought
this might cheer you up a notch.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:04.724
That's not necessary.

00:02:04.808 --> 00:02:08.811
What day is today?
It's Leela's birthday

00:02:08.896 --> 00:02:09.937
Please stop.

00:02:10.022 --> 00:02:12.982
What a day for a birthday

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.192
I really would like
you to stop singing.

00:02:15.277 --> 00:02:16.903
...cake!

00:02:16.987 --> 00:02:20.156
You want to buy a slice of
birthday cake for $11.95?

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:21.490
Yes, please.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:24.911
Ooh, nice cake.
Sorry, I'm late.

00:02:24.995 --> 00:02:27.538
Where have you...
It's fine.

00:02:27.664 --> 00:02:29.582
You're not mad?
I was.

00:02:29.666 --> 00:02:31.876
But then I realized
it's actually my fault

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.337
for thinking you might be on time for once.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.797
Anyhow,
I ate both our lunches.

00:02:36.924 --> 00:02:39.091
You ordered
the lobster pileup.

00:02:39.176 --> 00:02:40.176
It wasn't cheap.

00:02:41.762 --> 00:02:42.762
Bam!

00:02:47.225 --> 00:02:49.226
Please, let me
make it up to you.

00:02:49.311 --> 00:02:50.895
I'll treat you to
a fancy birthday dinner

00:02:50.979 --> 00:02:52.521
tonight, at Cavern
on the Green.

00:02:52.606 --> 00:02:55.650
Wow, that'll be the nicest
place I've ever been stood up.

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:56.859
Not this time.

00:02:56.944 --> 00:02:59.362
No matter what happens,
I swear I'll be there.

00:02:59.446 --> 00:03:02.615
Guys, guys! Hedonismbot is
finally gonna settle down,

00:03:02.699 --> 00:03:05.117
and marry a nice
house in the suburbs!

00:03:05.202 --> 00:03:10.456
But tonight, he's having the
girls-gone-wildest bachelor party of all time!

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.710
Who cares?
I'm having dinner with Leela.

00:03:16.046 --> 00:03:17.838
Just go to your
stupid party.

00:03:17.923 --> 00:03:20.341
We can have dinner on my birthday some other year.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.469
No! I can throw up
on a stripper anytime.

00:03:23.553 --> 00:03:27.181
Tonight, I want to
not throw up on you.

00:03:27.265 --> 00:03:28.432
Really?

00:03:28.517 --> 00:03:29.642
Your loss.

00:03:29.726 --> 00:03:32.311
Hey, Professor,
you're my wingman!

00:03:32.396 --> 00:03:36.232
Very well. Cubert,
fetch my drinking teeth.

00:03:41.488 --> 00:03:46.158
I just have to sign Leela's
birthday card. How do you spell X-O?

00:03:46.243 --> 00:03:48.285
It's a record-your-own-message
card.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.122
You don't sign it, you
leave a nude video greeting.

00:03:51.248 --> 00:03:52.540
Does it have to be nude?

00:03:52.791 --> 00:03:55.001
I guess not.
That never occurred to me.

00:03:55.085 --> 00:03:57.878
If I leave now, record a
birthday greeting on the way,

00:03:57.963 --> 00:04:00.047
score some fancy cologne
at the newsstand,

00:04:00.132 --> 00:04:01.632
I'll be exactly on time.

00:04:01.925 --> 00:04:03.843
You're not going anywhere!

00:04:03.927 --> 00:04:04.927
But I have a date.

00:04:05.012 --> 00:04:06.345
You were late this morning,

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.849
so you have to stay
and test my latest invention!

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:14.353
Behold!
A time-traveling machine!

00:04:15.564 --> 00:04:17.857
Time?
I can't go back there!

00:04:18.442 --> 00:04:21.861
But this time machine
only goes forward in time.

00:04:21.945 --> 00:04:24.530
That way you can't
accidentally change history,

00:04:24.614 --> 00:04:28.409
or do something disgusting, like
sleep with your own grandmother.

00:04:28.493 --> 00:04:29.994
I wouldn't want
to do that again.

00:04:30.078 --> 00:04:34.582
We're going to test it by going
forward in time one minute.

00:04:34.666 --> 00:04:35.708
Get in.

00:04:35.792 --> 00:04:37.710
Okay, hurry.
Let's get it over with.

00:04:37.794 --> 00:04:40.504
I can record Leela's birthday
card while we're in there.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.425
Happy birthday, Leela!

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:46.510
I'm really sorry
I'm gonna be one minute late,

00:04:46.595 --> 00:04:48.888
'cause we're testing the
professor's dumb time machine, but...

00:04:48.972 --> 00:04:51.724
Okay, I'll just
nudge us forward

00:04:51.808 --> 00:04:54.685
exactly one minute
into the... Whoa!

00:04:56.021 --> 00:04:57.313
My card!

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.444
Did we go too far?

00:05:03.528 --> 00:05:04.528
What time is it?

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:07.490
The year 10,000.

00:05:10.827 --> 00:05:12.119
Whoopsie.

00:05:17.459 --> 00:05:20.211
Oh, dear.
I mean, oh, my.

00:05:20.295 --> 00:05:21.754
The year 10,000?

00:05:21.838 --> 00:05:24.173
But I promised Leela
I'd be on time for dinner!

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.508
Relax, Fry.

00:05:25.592 --> 00:05:29.220
Everyone we ever knew died
thousands of years ago.

00:05:29.304 --> 00:05:33.224
Everyone we ever knew?
I never liked those guys.

00:05:41.691 --> 00:05:43.609
No! They did it!

00:05:43.735 --> 00:05:45.361
They blew it up!

00:05:45.695 --> 00:05:48.864
And then the apes blew up
their society, too!

00:05:48.949 --> 00:05:51.158
How could this happen?

00:05:51.243 --> 00:05:54.954
And then the birds took over
and ruined their society!

00:05:55.038 --> 00:05:59.333
And the cows, and then, I don't
know, is that a slug, maybe?

00:05:59.417 --> 00:06:01.627
No!

00:06:12.681 --> 00:06:14.682
While you await
your "friend,"

00:06:14.766 --> 00:06:18.477
allow me to read from a
prepared history of our cavern.

00:06:18.645 --> 00:06:20.688
"These unique rock formations

00:06:20.772 --> 00:06:24.483
"were created over millions
of years by mineral-rich water,

00:06:24.568 --> 00:06:26.861
"dripping from
pores in the ceiling.

00:06:26.945 --> 00:06:31.073
"Dripping and dripping,
year upon year,

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:34.368
"century upon century..."

00:06:34.452 --> 00:06:37.079
What day is today?

00:06:37.164 --> 00:06:40.040
Hey, aren't you the loser who got
stood up at my other restaurant?

00:06:40.125 --> 00:06:42.168
Just shut up and
bring me two dinners.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:49.258
Has anyone seen Fry's ass? It's
late for a date with my boot.

00:06:49.426 --> 00:06:50.467
Fry's not here.

00:06:50.552 --> 00:06:54.722
Obviously, he went to that pervert
party with Bender and the professor.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.599
Fry went to the party?

00:06:58.101 --> 00:07:00.227
We interrupt
Hypnotoad On Ice

00:07:00.312 --> 00:07:04.815
to bring you breaking coverage of the
disaster at Hedonismbot's bachelor party.

00:07:06.109 --> 00:07:10.237
Linda, what began as innocent
fun ended in tragedy tonight

00:07:10.322 --> 00:07:12.531
when a nuclear-powered
robot stripper

00:07:12.616 --> 00:07:15.034
suffered a catastrophic
reactor meltdown.

00:07:15.118 --> 00:07:17.119
There is only one survivor.

00:07:17.287 --> 00:07:20.372
Everywhere I looked,
there were piles of bodies.

00:07:20.457 --> 00:07:22.208
And then
the explosion struck.

00:07:25.545 --> 00:07:29.256
The three co-workers
I liked, all dead!

00:07:29.341 --> 00:07:32.885
Fry stood me up and died?
I'm so angry!

00:07:32.969 --> 00:07:37.306
I mean, I'm so sad!
But I'm still pretty angry!

00:07:37.432 --> 00:07:40.434
But also sad.
Can I be both?

00:07:40.518 --> 00:07:41.727
It's what he'd want.

00:07:41.811 --> 00:07:44.230
Then that's what I am!

00:07:52.322 --> 00:07:54.490
Man, the future is
a total craphole,

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:57.576
and whoever lives here is
a crap-faced sack of crap!

00:07:57.827 --> 00:07:58.911
No offense, fellas.

00:07:58.995 --> 00:08:00.246
Don't sweat it, man.

00:08:00.455 --> 00:08:03.082
I'll never
see Leela again.

00:08:03.166 --> 00:08:07.586
No, without a backwards time
machine, we're stuck in this craphole.

00:08:07.671 --> 00:08:09.004
Dude, give it a rest.

00:08:09.089 --> 00:08:10.589
Hold on. I've got it!

00:08:10.674 --> 00:08:14.260
We can't go back in time,
but we can keep going forward

00:08:14.344 --> 00:08:17.346
until people invent
the backwards time machine.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:19.682
And then we can go home.
Hit it.

00:08:20.725 --> 00:08:25.145
In the year 105,105

00:08:25.855 --> 00:08:28.899
If man is still alive

00:08:30.193 --> 00:08:32.611
If robot can survive

00:08:33.071 --> 00:08:36.740
They may find

00:08:37.867 --> 00:08:41.578
In the year 252,525

00:08:41.663 --> 00:08:45.291
The backwards time machine
still won't have arrived

00:08:45.375 --> 00:08:49.169
In all the world
there's only one technology

00:08:49.254 --> 00:08:52.881
A rusty sword for
practicing proctology

00:08:53.383 --> 00:08:56.885
In a future year
that ends with a 20

00:08:56.970 --> 00:09:00.973
A shlubby merman's
gonna try to get chummy

00:09:01.057 --> 00:09:04.351
He may look
like a watery wimp

00:09:04.769 --> 00:09:08.689
When in fact he's
a bloodthirsty shrimp

00:09:08.773 --> 00:09:12.067
In the year one
million and a half

00:09:12.694 --> 00:09:16.405
Humankind is
enslaved by giraffe

00:09:16.489 --> 00:09:20.284
Man must pay for
all his misdeeds

00:09:20.368 --> 00:09:23.078
When the treetops
are stripped of their leaves

00:09:33.506 --> 00:09:35.758
Sometimes I can't
believe how successful

00:09:35.842 --> 00:09:38.510
Planet Express became
once the professor was killed

00:09:38.595 --> 00:09:39.845
and you seized control.

00:09:39.929 --> 00:09:42.681
There were tough times,
but we all pulled together.

00:09:42.766 --> 00:09:44.224
I've been crunching
the numbers

00:09:44.309 --> 00:09:45.934
on our
trans-galactic strategy...

00:09:46.019 --> 00:09:49.480
What are you doing here?
I laid you off 20 years ago.

00:09:52.609 --> 00:09:55.361
The claws can't flee
like they used to.

00:09:55.945 --> 00:09:59.615
Success is nice, but I do
kind of miss the old days.

00:10:03.995 --> 00:10:05.120
Hey, Leels.

00:10:06.247 --> 00:10:07.664
Hi, Cubert.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.051
May we help you,
strange ones?

00:10:19.135 --> 00:10:22.054
We are travelers from the past, my good runt.

00:10:22.138 --> 00:10:27.101
I see. Since your time,
human evolution has diverged.

00:10:27.685 --> 00:10:31.980
There are we, advanced
in intellect and morality.

00:10:32.232 --> 00:10:36.568
And the Dumblocks, stupid, vicious
brutes who live underground.

00:10:36.653 --> 00:10:38.821
Advanced in intellect,
you say?

00:10:38.905 --> 00:10:41.824
Have you invented
a backwards time machine?

00:10:41.908 --> 00:10:44.785
No, but if we apply
our superior minds,

00:10:44.869 --> 00:10:47.663
we could perfect such a device within five years.

00:10:47.831 --> 00:10:49.206
See you then!

00:10:54.087 --> 00:10:55.879
We're back for
our time machine!

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.090
Ow!

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.683
Yoo-hoo! Boys!

00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:10.436
What's this era in
human history like?

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:14.231
The machines. We built them
to make our lives easier,

00:11:14.315 --> 00:11:15.482
but they rebelled.

00:11:15.567 --> 00:11:18.819
They won't stop until every human is dead.

00:11:18.903 --> 00:11:21.822
This seems like a nice
future. Let's just stay here.

00:11:21.906 --> 00:11:25.033
We could settle down
on that mountain of skulls.

00:11:27.245 --> 00:11:30.789
Hey! That place had a
gorgeous view of Blood Lake!

00:11:34.294 --> 00:11:35.878
Greetings, time travelers.

00:11:35.962 --> 00:11:39.131
Stupid jerks! Wouldn't let
me stay in the good future.

00:11:39.215 --> 00:11:41.008
How did you know
we're time travelers?

00:11:41.092 --> 00:11:43.802
We, too, study
the time-travel enigma.

00:11:43.887 --> 00:11:47.598
We have perfected a method using
negative-mass neutrino fields

00:11:47.974 --> 00:11:50.809
that allows us to
travel backwards in time.

00:11:50.894 --> 00:11:52.311
My name's Hubert.

00:11:52.395 --> 00:11:54.146
All right!
We can go home!

00:11:57.025 --> 00:11:59.026
We can talk of our
research tomorrow.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.361
Men are very rare
in our society.

00:12:01.446 --> 00:12:04.323
Even very old and
stupid males are prized.

00:12:04.407 --> 00:12:08.160
Tonight, please be the guests of
honor at our fertility banquet.

00:12:08.244 --> 00:12:12.331
Well, there's certainly no
harm in a fertility banquet.

00:12:12.415 --> 00:12:14.333
I could eat.
And fertilize.

00:12:14.417 --> 00:12:19.254
Very well. Let us anoint our guests
in oil without using our hands.

00:12:19.339 --> 00:12:23.509
So, we can stay in the future you
like, but not the future I like?

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:24.927
Next!

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:28.764
No! I was about
to close the deal!

00:12:28.848 --> 00:12:31.350
Bender, they had
a backwards time machine!

00:12:31.434 --> 00:12:33.685
The other place had
a lot of good things, too!

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.687
Did you even see
that mountain of skulls?

00:12:35.772 --> 00:12:37.064
Why, you!

00:12:38.149 --> 00:12:39.608
Oh, no, you didn't.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:45.739
Stop! Somewhere, sometime,
Leela is waiting for me.

00:12:45.823 --> 00:12:48.450
We need to keep looking
for a backwards time machine.

00:12:48.535 --> 00:12:49.576
Fry's right.

00:12:49.661 --> 00:12:52.829
Yes. We have to work
together, not have this fight,

00:12:52.914 --> 00:12:54.581
which I was
definitely winning.

00:12:56.793 --> 00:12:58.377
The year one billion.

00:12:58.545 --> 00:13:00.420
I've got a feeling
this could be exactly

00:13:00.505 --> 00:13:03.131
the point in time
we've been looking for!

00:13:04.676 --> 00:13:05.717
Nope.

00:13:08.805 --> 00:13:11.723
In fact,
all life is extinct.

00:13:13.059 --> 00:13:14.560
So let's keep going forward.

00:13:14.644 --> 00:13:17.729
It's no use.
Earth is dead.

00:13:17.814 --> 00:13:20.816
This is the end
of all things.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.334
The Cavern on the Green.

00:13:44.132 --> 00:13:46.049
I made it, Leela.

00:13:46.259 --> 00:13:48.552
Sorry I'm
a billion years late.

00:14:02.317 --> 00:14:05.444
You'll get your alimony
check, Cubert. Now get lost!

00:14:05.528 --> 00:14:08.614
Chill out.
I'm just here to see Amy.

00:14:08.698 --> 00:14:13.035
Move it, boy toy. Granny's
taking you to Atlantic City.

00:14:16.372 --> 00:14:18.957
I don't know why you ever
married that pig-nosed punk.

00:14:19.042 --> 00:14:21.960
I don't know, either.
I'm married to the job now.

00:14:22.045 --> 00:14:25.339
I used to think there was
someone for me, but... Ow!

00:14:26.382 --> 00:14:30.844
How odd. It's one of those old
record-your-own-message birthday cards.

00:14:32.221 --> 00:14:33.555
Happy birthday, Leela!

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.474
I'm really sorry
I'm gonna be one minute late,

00:14:35.558 --> 00:14:37.976
'cause we're testing the
professor's dumb time machine...

00:14:38.061 --> 00:14:41.688
But, you know,
happy birthday and all, and,

00:14:42.398 --> 00:14:45.734
I love you.
My card!

00:14:49.572 --> 00:14:54.326
My whole life I've been mad at
him, and it wasn't his fault.

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:55.512
You know, all in all,
I had a good life.

00:15:55.596 --> 00:15:57.389
What do you say the three of us grab a six-pack

00:15:57.473 --> 00:15:59.057
and watch
the universe end?

00:15:59.142 --> 00:16:00.225
Hear! Hear!

00:16:00.309 --> 00:16:02.436
That's basically
what I do every day.

00:16:05.648 --> 00:16:07.816
To the end of the universe!

00:16:21.581 --> 00:16:24.791
So long, Earth. Thanks for the air and whatnot.

00:16:32.508 --> 00:16:33.759
Whoa!
Whoa!

00:16:34.552 --> 00:16:37.262
Hey, what was the
purpose of life anyway?

00:16:37.346 --> 00:16:41.600
Who knows? Probably some
hogwash about the human spirit.

00:16:41.684 --> 00:16:42.809
Sounds about right.

00:16:46.189 --> 00:16:48.148
The stars
are receding.

00:16:48.399 --> 00:16:51.067
Oh, the vast emptiness!

00:16:52.195 --> 00:16:54.654
Yeah, yeah,
I can take a hint.

00:16:59.535 --> 00:17:02.871
The last proton should be decaying about now.

00:17:02.955 --> 00:17:04.372
Bye, last proton.

00:17:04.624 --> 00:17:09.377
And, here we are.
The end of the universe.

00:17:17.261 --> 00:17:19.763
Well, now what?
You guys want to talk?

00:17:19.847 --> 00:17:20.889
No, thanks.

00:17:23.893 --> 00:17:25.143
Did anyone else see that?

00:17:25.228 --> 00:17:26.394
Unbelievable!

00:17:26.479 --> 00:17:28.730
It's a second big bang!

00:17:34.695 --> 00:17:37.697
My God, is it possible?

00:17:37.782 --> 00:17:39.866
It must be possible.
It's happening.

00:17:39.951 --> 00:17:41.660
By the way,
what's happening?

00:17:41.744 --> 00:17:46.331
It appears this universe is
exactly identical to the old one.

00:17:46.415 --> 00:17:49.960
If so, we just need to keep going forward in time

00:17:50.044 --> 00:17:51.753
to the point when we left!

00:17:56.592 --> 00:17:58.426
The Earth is born!

00:18:04.934 --> 00:18:07.978
Ladies and gentlemen,
the moon!

00:18:08.437 --> 00:18:10.939
Look. The first fish
to crawl up on land.

00:18:12.316 --> 00:18:14.359
It was coming right at us!
You saw it.

00:18:14.485 --> 00:18:16.611
I'm gonna grab
another beer.

00:18:17.196 --> 00:18:19.781
Fry, Fry, you're missing the dinosaurs!

00:18:19.866 --> 00:18:22.492
It's okay.
They're not going anywhere.

00:18:23.119 --> 00:18:24.286
Where'd they go?

00:18:32.461 --> 00:18:33.795
Now, what's going on there?

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:34.921
History.

00:18:35.006 --> 00:18:37.549
Hang on. I just want to make one stop.

00:19:03.326 --> 00:19:05.368
Easy, easy.

00:19:05.661 --> 00:19:07.746
Taking her in
for a landing.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:11.041
One year to go.
Six months.

00:19:11.125 --> 00:19:12.500
I'm almost there, Leela.

00:19:12.585 --> 00:19:15.921
One month,
two weeks, one hour,

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:20.300
30 seconds, and here we...

00:19:20.384 --> 00:19:21.760
Whoa!

00:19:22.261 --> 00:19:24.387
Stop!
Give me the keys, Magoo!

00:19:28.684 --> 00:19:30.727
We'll have to
bring her around again.

00:19:42.031 --> 00:19:44.950
Just slow it down. I'll
shoot Hitler out the window.

00:19:46.369 --> 00:19:49.496
Darn! I hit Eleanor
Roosevelt by mistake.

00:19:49.872 --> 00:19:52.832
Okay,
nearing our era again.

00:19:53.209 --> 00:19:57.045
Here we go.
Careful this time.

00:19:57.588 --> 00:19:59.047
Careful.

00:19:59.215 --> 00:20:02.842
We're going to test it by going
forward in time one minute.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.302
Get in.

00:20:04.387 --> 00:20:06.388
Okay. Hurry.
Let's get it over with.

00:20:08.391 --> 00:20:09.391
Uh-oh.

00:20:09.475 --> 00:20:13.186
This new universe is about 10
feet lower than our old one.

00:20:16.565 --> 00:20:20.026
Pow! We took care of
the time travel paradox.

00:20:20.111 --> 00:20:21.569
All right!
Hooray!

00:20:22.321 --> 00:20:24.406
Uh-oh. I'm late for
dinner with Leela.

00:20:27.827 --> 00:20:29.327
Welcome to
Cavern on the Green.

00:20:29.412 --> 00:20:32.455
May I offer you some meat loaf while you wait?

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:33.832
Sorry I'm late!

00:20:33.916 --> 00:20:35.625
Actually, you're on time.

00:20:36.043 --> 00:20:37.085
Really?

00:20:37.169 --> 00:20:40.588
I have to admit, I was
afraid you wouldn't make it.

00:20:40.673 --> 00:20:43.842
That was the old Fry.
He's dead now.

00:20:45.761 --> 00:20:47.303
Happy birthday, Leela.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:50.181
I got you a card, but I guess I kind of lost it.

00:20:50.246 --> 00:20:52.831
That's okay.
I don't really like cards.

00:20:52.935 --> 00:20:55.645
What I'll remember is
our time together.